From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Radsat Developers <dev@radsat.local>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:55:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] spi: omap3: BBB SPI1 D0=MISO D1=MOSI

Non-DM omap3_spi defaulted to D0_OUT_D1_IN. RadSat wiring / Linux
beaglebone-black.dts uses D0 as MISO and D1 as MOSI, so U-Boot could
write (or appear to) while reads returned garbage and env CRC failed.
Match Linux pin direction.

---

diff --git a/drivers/spi/omap3_spi.c b/drivers/spi/omap3_spi.c
--- a/drivers/spi/omap3_spi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/omap3_spi.c
@@ -569,7 +569,11 @@
 	priv->mode = mode;
 	priv->wordlen = priv->slave.wordlen;
 #ifdef CONFIG_OMAP3_SPI_D0_D1_SWAPPED
-	priv->pin_dir = MCSPI_PINDIR_D0_OUT_D1_IN;
+	/*
+	 * RadSat BBB SPI1 (spidev1.0): D0=MISO, D1=MOSI — matches Linux
+	 * beaglebone-black.dts spi1_pins (0x194 input, 0x198 output).
+	 */
+	priv->pin_dir = MCSPI_PINDIR_D0_IN_D1_OUT;
 #endif
 
 	return &priv->slave;
